A||N||9||BlackDragon||what would cause a vehicle to not start. o/t||||1||
Z||000000||BlackDragon||08-13-2001||11:26 PM||||this is not a fiero, but it is a technical question. i have a jeep wagoneer....(POS).. it starts perfectly sometimes, but other times, it will turn over for 5 minutes strait, and still not start. i dont think it is a fuel prob. it has nothing to do with temperature. I have replaced plugs and wires, i dont know what to do now. any input would be helpful||||reg||1
Z||000001||MD_Fiero||08-13-2001||11:43 PM||||well, this is a prett vague question you see...<P><BR>their are tons upon tons of things that could make a car(such as yours) not start....the biggest thing, to the smallest thing in the vehicle.<P>this question can't really be answer'd unless it was narrowed down to smaller questions.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackDragon||08-13-2001||11:50 PM||||once it starts, it runs perfect. no miss or anything. it turns over fine even when it will not start. it is fuel injected l-6. is there any other info that will help at all?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||08-13-2001||11:57 PM||||Like he said it could be a lot of things. I'll just throw a couple of ideas out.<P>1. Ignition timing.<P>2. A "weak" starter. I had a chevy truck one time that acted a lot like that. It <B>sounded</B> like it was turning over fine but apparently it was spinning just a little slow. Changed the starter and it started first time every time...||||reg||1
Z||000004||BlackDragon||08-14-2001||12:01 AM||||thanks, that at least gives me somewhere to start, any other suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||08-14-2001||01:17 AM||||When does this problem usually occur? Both when hot and cold? Narrow it down. When you realize it is going to take a while starting, maybe check for spark right then. If it has spark, still won't start, chk fuel pressure. Don't know if you can on the waggoneer, but maybe squirt of gas in the intake. If it starts then, it's fuel related.Could even be something like a faulty ign switch, bad elec connection.||||reg||1
Z||000006||TylerB11||08-14-2001||12:18 PM||||Fuel Pump. Check it out. I had a jeep that did the same thing, the fuel pump was going and it would run fine, but have trouble starting sometimes.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BlackDragon||08-14-2001||07:49 PM||||thnx for input once again. will try all suggestions. doesnt matter if it is hot or cold, symptoms hold firm in both conditions. dont know if this matters or not, but the engine overheats if idles too long, it likes to be run kinda hard||||reg||1
Z||000008||BlackDragon||08-14-2001||07:52 PM||||fuel injected, so cant pour fuel in it||||reg||1
Z||000009||87GTBro||08-14-2001||08:52 PM||||You can still put fuel in the intake on a fuel injected engine.  It will suck the fuel into the cylinder regardless...  wont work as good but still works.  The best way is to get someone to spray carb cleaner into the mouth of the intake while you are cranking the engine.<P>If it turns over or tries to start while spraying the cleaner, then you are not getting fuel (check the fuel pump).  If it still doesnt turn over or try to start then you have an ignition problem.  In that case I would check the distributor cap, rotor, ignition coil and ignition module.<P>Hope that helps!<P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
